1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,510
Is the dot product
a shadow's length?

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:06,430
Two arrows (vectors), a and b

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,000
Shine light straight down onto a,
and b casts a shadow on a

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:11,770
Dot product = length of a × length of the shadow

5
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:14,140
Let's change the angle

6
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:17,910
Same direction: the shadow is longest

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:21,480
At a right angle the shadow is 0 → the dot product is 0

8
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:25,350
Lean past it to the other side and it's negative!

9
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,520
Shadow length = |b| cos θ
(the sideways shadow from the sin·cos episode!)

10
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:32,020
When you pull a sled at an angle,
the force that moves it forward = the shadow

11
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:36,770
NEXT: An infinite proof
with dominoes
